      },
      "message": "feat(sim): one eikonal sweep re-normalizes the render lattice's band\n\nFieldLattice::renormalize runs one cycle of fast sweeping (Zhao 2005:\nGodunov upwind update, Gauss-Seidel over the eight sweep orders) over\nthe packed lattice's narrow band, so the sphere-traced view's shading\ngradient reads |grad phi| ~ 1 where the BFS magnitudes and the cut\nlayer's CSG max leave it bent. PackedBase::of calls it before the\nrender pass's upload.\n\n- The surface never moves: every texel with a 26-neighbour of the\n  other sign is frozen bit for bit, every other texel keeps its sign.\n- Band only: texels at or past cap are untouched; solved magnitudes\n  clamp at cap. Cost is 8 x band texels updates, deterministic.\n- The cut layer stays as packed (the composed value goes into the mesh\n  layer), so playback's later cut layers only lift cells over it.\n- Display only: the verdict paths keep reading the sparse field.\n\nPinned by tests/stock_eikonal.rs: CSG cuts' mean | |grad| - 1 | drops\n0.367 -> 0.048 (bound 0.08, 83% of texels within 0.1); every texel\nkeeps its sign and every zero-crossing edge keeps both values; a\ncylinder pocket agrees with its closed-form distance within 0.21 at a\n0.5 cell; a plane reads exact; out-of-band texels untouched;\ndeterministic; a mismatched lattice refuses unchanged.\n\nFixes #22\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
